  "notes": "Composed of {荷|に} (cargo/freight) and {積|づ}み (loading/stacking, from {積|つ}む). Refers specifically to the process of loading goods onto a transport vehicle. The opposite operation is {荷降|にお}ろし (unloading).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {荷積|にづ}み{作業|さぎょう}: loading work\n- {荷積|にづ}みを{行|おこな}う: to carry out loading\n- {荷積|にづ}み{場所|ばしょ}: loading area\n- トラックに{荷積|にづ}みする: to load onto a truck\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {積|つ}み{込|こ}み: loading, stowing — similar but emphasizes putting items into a container or vehicle\n- {荷降|にお}ろし: unloading — the reverse process of removing cargo\n- {積載|せきさい}: loading, carrying — a more formal/technical term for carrying a load",
